{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"reasoning","text":"Interesting! There are several problems:\n\n1. Many marker genes are \"missing\" — not present in sym2idx (the set of gene symbols). MBP, TUBB3, OLIG2, etc. — wait, they existed in the `allflat` set before! The problem: sym2idx is keyed on the primary (first) symbol of each gene, but MBP etc. are secondary [hs] symbols (the first symbol is an nr symbol like \"LOC...\" or some other name). My interval construction only aggregated by the first symbol. I need to map all symbols of a gene to that gene's accessibility. So I need a symbol → gene index mapping (many-to-one), where each marker symbol resolves to the primary symbol of the gene that contains it.\n\nIn scratch_gtf_syms.py, syms was keyed on parts[0] with the full set attached. In step 1, only symbols[0] was saved. Fix: for each gene, keep all symbols; build a map symbol → primary symbol (or a list of gene primary symbols). Then marker resolution will work.\n\n2. The \"nan\" self_z for Pancreas, Intestine, Cloaca, Prostate, Limb is because some marker genes had sd=0 (no variance across organs → nan z). This is fine — use nanmean.\n\n3. The argmax mismatches are partially artifacts of the missing markers. Let me fix symbol resolution and re-run. Also handle nan in z with nanmean, and count the number of valid markers.\n\nAlso note that Stomach's argmax is Cloaca, and GallBladder's argmax is Prostate — could be real signal or noise. Let me fix it first.\n\nFix: build sym_map: all symbols → primary symbol of that gene (if multiple genes share a marker symbol, average across those genes' primary symbols — e.g., multiple INS paralogs). Let me redo step 1 to keep all symbols per gene and create an all-symbol → gene-primary-symbol map."}}
