{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"reasoning","text":"Now this is highly suggestive. Let me try to interpret the top genes of each column:\n\n- **Brain column**: STMN4, JAKMIP2, CACNG8, LHFPL4, SPOCK2, NPTXR, BRSK1, GRIN2B, SEZ6L2, KCNJ9 — all neuronal/synaptic ✓ genuine brain.\n- **Heart column**: SBK2, LSMEM2, HSPB1, TRIM54, MYO18B, LRRC10, ACTN3, GDF10, DUSP27, ALPK3, MYLK4, TECRL, TTN — all cardiac/muscle ✓ genuine heart.\n- **Liver column**: OIT3, FETUB, TMPRSS6, CA6, F7, TAT, SERPIND1, MASP2, PROZ, SPP2, LEAP2, FGB, AGT, TF-A — all liver ✓ genuine.\n- **Pancreas column**: CELA1, CTRL, CELA2A, CEL, PRSS2, CPB1, SYCN, ERP27 — all pancreatic digestive enzymes ✓ genuine.\n- **Spleen column**: DCC, CXCR5, CD72, POU2AF1, RAG2, RAG1, FLT3 — all lymphoid/immune ✓ genuine spleen.\n- **Lung column**: EVA1A, SFTPC, MIXL1... SFTPC is there ✓ genuine lung.\n- **Kidney column**: SLC34A1 (NPT2a — proximal tubule!), SLC23A3, SLC26A1, ACOT12, PAX8 — kidney ✓ genuine! PAX8 and SLC34A1 are definitive proximal tubule markers. So the kidney column is genuine kidney. (The earlier \"Kidney marker argmax=Gill\" was driven by noisy markers NPHS2/LRP2/GATA3 etc., not the core program.)\n- **Intestine column**: NXPE4, SLC15A1, CDHR2, SI, TM4SF20, CD36, SLC7A9, PDZK1 — brush border/absorptive enterocyte ✓ genuine intestine.\n- **Cloaca column**: CLDN18.S, TFF3.2, TM4SF1, VSIG2 — TFF3 is a trefoil factor (intestinal mucosa), CLDN18 tight junction... hmm, cloaca is gut-like ✓ reasonable.\n- **Bladder column**: AQP-T2 (aquaporin!), C2CD5, PREX2, METTL21C, MYH3, ROBO4... AQP-T2 is aquaporin (kidney/urinary). Hmm — AQP-T2? Is this aquaporin? \"AQP-T2\" sounds like an amphibian aquaporin. MYH3 is muscle (bladder smooth muscle!). ROBO4 is endothelial. Bladder is plausible but the markers are weak.\n- **Limb column**: DCT (dopachrome tautomerase — melanocyte!), TNFSF13B, TNFAIP6, PRRX1 (limb mesenchyme!), C1QTNF5... DCT = melanocyte pigment cell. Axolotl limb skin has melano